cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Si usas este atlas, cítalo así / If you use this atlas, please cite it as below."
title: "Atlas EM/SFC: atlas interactivo de la literatura sobre encefalomielitis miálgica / síndrome de fatiga crónica (2010–2026)"
authors:
  - family-names: "Giraldo Lozano"
    given-names: "Celeste"
type: software
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-21
url: "https://celestediwind.github.io/atlas-mecfs/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CelesteDiWind/atlas-mecfs"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - ME/CFS
  - myalgic encephalomyelitis
  - chronic fatigue syndrome
  - long COVID
  - bibliometrics
  - science mapping
  - citation networks
  - persistent homology
  - OpenAlex
abstract: >-
  Interactive map of the ME/CFS research literature, 2010–2026: a hand-picked selection of 583 papers and a systematic
  corpus of 7,169 OpenAlex works, with topic analyses, an analysis of the field (structure, dialogue between topics,
  change over time) and topic syntheses. Conceived, designed and directed by Celeste Giraldo Lozano, with the assistance of Claude (Anthropic) for implementation.
